[ar:MP3 同步字幕版（美音）]
[ti:Porpoises]
[by:更多学习内容，请到VeryCD.com搜索“露珠”]
[00:00.88]Lesson 18 | 第18课
[00:02.80]Porpoises | 海豚
[00:09.00]What would you say is the main characteristic of porpoises? | 你认为海豚的主要特征是什么？
[00:15.63]There has long been a superstition among mariners that porpoises will save drowning men by pushing them to the surface, | 长期以来，海员中流传着一种迷信，说海豚会把溺水的人推到水面使之获救，
[00:23.59]or protect them from sharks by surrounding them in defensive formation. | 或者围成防御队形保护他们不受鲨鱼的伤害。
[00:29.17]Marine Studio biologists have pointed out that, however intelligent they may be, | 海洋摄影室的生物学家指出，无论海豚多么聪明，
[00:34.75]it is probably a mistake to credit dolphins with any motive of life-saving. | 认为它们有救人的动机可能是错误的。
[00:40.59]On the occasions when they have pushed to shore an unconscious human being they have much more likely done it out of curiosity or for sport, | 在它们把失去知觉的人推到岸边的情况下，它们多半是出于好奇或为了游戏，
[00:49.66]as in riding the bow waves of a ship. | 就像它们追逐船首的波浪一样。
[00:53.49]In 1928 some porpoises were photographed working like beavers to push ashore a waterlogged mattress. | 1928年，有人拍到几只海豚像海狸一样把一张浸透水的床垫推上岸。
[01:01.70]If, as has been reported, they have protected humans from sharks, | 如果真如报道所说它们保护过人类免遭鲨鱼伤害，
[01:06.35]it may have been because curiosity attracted them and because the scent of a possible meal attracted the sharks. | 那可能是因为好奇心吸引了海豚，而一顿美餐的气味吸引了鲨鱼。
[01:14.03]Porpoises and sharks are natural enemies. | 海豚和鲨鱼是天敌。
[01:17.32]It is possible that upon such an occasion a battle ensued, with the sharks being driven away or killed. | 可能在这样的场合发生了一场搏斗，鲨鱼被赶走或被咬死。
[01:24.97]Whether it be bird, fish or beast, the porpoise is intrigued with anything that is alive. | 无论是鸟、鱼还是兽，海豚对任何活的东西都感兴趣。
[01:31.85]They are constantly after the turtles, who peacefully submit to all sorts of indignities. | 它们经常追逐海龟，而海龟则温顺地忍受着种种凌辱。
[01:37.78]One young calf especially enjoyed raising a turtle to the surface with his snout, | 一只小海豚特别喜欢用鼻子把海龟顶到水面，
[01:43.53]and then shoving him across the tank like an aquaplane. | 然后像滑水板一样把它推过水池。
[01:48.38]Almost any day a young porpoises may be seen trying to turn a 300-pound sea turtle over by sticking his snout under the edge of his shell and pushing up for dear life. | 几乎随便哪一天，你都可以看到一只小海豚把鼻子伸到一只300磅重的海龟的甲壳边缘下面，拼命地往上顶，试图把它翻过来。
[02:00.82]This is not easy, and may require two porpoises working together. | 这可不容易，可能需要两只海豚合力进行。
[02:06.35]In another game, as the turtle swims across the oceanarium, the first porpoise swoops down from above and butts his shell with his belly. | 在另一种游戏中，当海龟游过海洋馆时，第一只海豚从上方猛扑下来，用腹部撞击龟壳。
[02:16.45]This knocks the turtle down several feet. | 这一下把海龟撞下去好几英尺。
[02:19.67]He no sooner recovers his equilibrium than the next porpoises comes along and hits him another crack. | 它刚恢复平衡，下一只海豚又赶上来再给它狠狠一击。
[02:27.25]Eventually the turtle has been butted all the way down to the floor of the tank. | 最后，海龟被一路撞到池底。
[02:33.07]He is now satisfied merely to try to stand up, but as soon as he does so a porpoise knocks him flat. | 这时它只要试图站起来就满足了，但它刚一站起来，一只海豚就把它撞倒。
[02:41.12]The turtle at last gives up by pulling his feet under his shell and the game is over. | 海龟最终把脚缩进壳里放弃了抵抗，游戏到此结束。
